164	          <div class="area-desc">Claude drove large spec-driven TDD pipelines for Rust crates, dispatching sub-agents to implement SPEC-005 through SPEC-009 against strict exit gates. Work involved repeated fix-and-reconfirm cycles when gates returned FAIL verdicts, including field-type pinning issues and surviving mutants from mutation testing. Task tracking tools and agent delegation were used heavily to keep long multi-step plans moving to green test counts.</div>
