172	          <div class="area-desc">The user handed Claude a pre-approved 45-task remediation plan for a Rust monorepo and asked it to run to completion autonomously. Claude sequentially landed tasks with passing tests across many files, using Bash and Edit for the bulk of the work. A mid-session hygiene lapse—spec JSON and plan docs believed committed but never actually committed—required repo-state verification and reconstituting a two-commit split.</div>
