  "description": "The session's real, native conversation/thread identifier (Claude Code's requestId, Codex's thread_id, Antigravity's conversation-id-as-directory-name), populated at parse time by the lumen-session adapter from a source-native field -- singular, matching the real OTel gen_ai.conversation.id attribute's actual per-session cardinality (verified directly against github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions-genai's model/gen-ai/registry.yaml), not a collected list. Replaces both otel_request_ids (wrong shape -- a session has one conversation id, not a small accumulated list) and, together with CanonicalToolCall/CanonicalToolResult.call_id, the removed otel_span_id/SpanMappingAccumulator (redundant -- the real gen_ai.tool.call.id attribute is functionally identical to Lumen's pre-existing call_id field, confirmed by direct comparison against the same registry; no new correlation mechanism was needed).",
  "error_conditions": [
    "MUST be None when the source has no native conversation/thread id available -- per the real registry's own explicit rule, a fallback UUID, trace id, or content hash SHALL NOT be synthesized as a substitute."
  ]
},
