nfirms Lumen's Tarjan-SCC approach is directionally sound and, in one real dimension, MORE general (arbitrary-length cycles vs. OpenHands' fixed patterns) -- but OpenHands covers two failure categories Tarjan-SCC has no equivalent of: agent monologue (no user interruption for N consecutive turns) and live mid-loop intervention (a corrective nudge, not just post-hoc detection). No criteria are added for these here -- flagged as a possible follow-up spec addition if the user wants monologue/error-streak detection, not added speculatively without that decision."
