    "id": "CRIT-LUMEN-070",
    "criterion": "WHEN a transcript contains 3 identical CodeSearch invocations sharing the same query (which grounds to target_symbol per ground_tool_intent, lib.rs:196-205) without interleaving mutations, THE SYSTEM SHALL identify a Tarjan SCC cyclic loop and emit a CircularLoopAnomaly.",
    "is_error_case": false,
    "judgment_call": false,
    "reasoning": "Fixed two audit-confirmed defects (2026-08-20): (1) the real emitted type is CircularLoopAnomaly (lib.rs:18, api_surface line 19-23), not \"CycleAnomaly\" -- the wrong name was also independently leaking into SPEC-LUMEN-007-INSIGHTS's FindingGenerator signature, fixed there too. (2) The example was changed from a FileRead-based scenario (3 identical view_file invocations) to a CodeSearch-based one, because detect_circular_loops (lib.rs:88-107) only checks target_symbol for redundancy, never target_file -- confirmed by direct code read. FileRead/FileEdit ground exclusively on target_file (ground_tool_intent, lib.rs:198-199), so a repeated-FileRead cycle as originally worded would NOT actually be detected by current code; the example must use a tool that grounds on target_symbol (CodeSearch) to be a true statement. File-based redundancy detection (repeated reads of the same file) is a real, currently undetected gap -- not fixed here since it requires a lib.rs code change (checking target_symbol.or(target_file) rather than target_symbol alone), out of scope for a specs-only pass; tracked as a follow-up."
  },
  {
    "id": "CRIT-LUMEN-071",
    "criterion": "WHEN calculate_monotonicity is invoked on a transcript where detect_circular_loops returns an empty Vec (no set of >= 3 tool invocations sharing an identical grounded target_symbol with no interleaving mutation, per CRIT-LUMEN-070), THE SYSTEM SHALL return M = 1.0.",
    "is_error_case": false,
    "judgment_call": false,
    "reasoning": "\"Zero backtracking\" was never defined anywhere in the spec (audit finding, 2026-08-20); rewritten to bind precisely to detect_circular_loops's actual empty-result condition, consistent with how CRIT-LUMEN-155 already describes the non-empty case."
  },
  {
    "id": "CRIT-LUMEN-072",
    "criterion": "WHEN compute_recovery_index(transcript) is invoked on a transcript where an error occurs on turn i and no error occurs on turn i+1 (1 adaptive error pivot out of 1 total error event), THE SYSTEM SHALL return Error Recovery Index R = adaptive_error_pivots / total_error_events = 1.0.",
    "is_error_case": false,
    "judgment_call": false
  },
  {
    "id": "CRIT-LUMEN-073",
    "criterion": "WHEN compute_grounding_score(transcript) is invoked on a transcript with N total tool calls where G of them are FileRead/FileEdit calls with a non-empty path or CodeSearch calls with a non-empty query (every other ToolIntent variant -- FileCreate, FileDiscovery, TestExecution, VersionControl, SubagentSpawn, McpCall, Other -- counts as grounded unconditionally, per the real implementation), THE SYSTEM SHALL return G = grounded_tools / N.",
    "is_error_case": false,
    "judgment_call": false,
    "reasoning": "The prior wording (\"grounded in prior user or tool outputs versus hallucinated values\") both contradicted the api_surface's own stated formula (G = Grounded/Total Invocations, not Grounded/Hallucinated) and did not match the real implementation (lib.rs:131-161), which checks only for a non-empty path/query on 3 ToolIntent variants and treats every other variant as automatically grounded -- it never actually checks grounding against prior turns' outputs (audit finding, 2026-08-20). Rewritten to describe the real, buildable heuristic precisely, following the same bind-to-real-formula pattern already used for CRIT-LUMEN-072. If \"grounded against prior turn output\" is the intended long-term semantic, that requires an implementation change, not just a criterion rewording -- flagged, not silently absorbed into this wording."
  },
  {
    "id": "CRIT-LUMEN-074",
    "criterion": "IF a transcript has 0 or 1 turns, THE SYSTEM SHALL return monotonicity M = 1.0 and grounding score = 1.0 without dividing by zero.",
    "is_error_case": true,
    "judgment_call": false
  },
  {
    "id": "CRIT-LUMEN-155",
    "criterion": "WHEN calculate_monotonicity(transcript) is invoked on a transcript containing 3 consecutive tool invocations that share the same grounded target file or symbol with no interleaving mutation, THE SYSTEM SHALL return M < 1.0, reflecting a detected circular exploration loop.",
    "is_error_case": false,
    "judgment_call": false,
    "reasoning": "Status update, 2026-08-20: TrajectoryGraph now has a target_last_seen map (lib.rs:37-42) that closes a back-edge on target revisit, so push_tool no longer produces a strictly linear chain -- the 'known-failing (red)' status this criterion's spec-level reasoning previously described is stale; back-edge construction has since been implemented. This criterion itself is unchanged (its wording was already correct), only the historical status note elsewhere in this file needed correcting."
  },
  {
    "id": "CRIT-LUMEN-170",
    "criterion": "WHEN TrajectoryGraph::calculate_efficiency is invoked, THE SYSTEM SHALL return (total_mutations + total_reads * 0.5) / (total_mutations + total_reads); IF total_mutations + total_reads == 0, THE SYSTEM SHALL return 1.0 without dividing by zero.",
    "is_error_case": false,
    "judgment_call": false,
    "reasoning": "calculate_efficiency was declared in api_surface and implemented (lib.rs:109-115, with its own zero-division guard) but had zero acceptance criteria and was missing from scope -- audit finding, 2026-08-20. Both gaps fixed: added to scope above, and a criterion binding to the real weighted formula (mutation weight 1.0, read weight 0.5) plus its zero-division guard added here."
  },
  {
    "id": "CRIT-LUMEN-171",
    "criterion": "IF a Tarjan SCC component has exactly 2 nodes sharing an identical target_symbol with no interleaving mutation, THE SYSTEM SHALL NOT emit a CircularLoopAnomaly for it -- the >= 3 threshold in CRIT-LUMEN-070 is a strict lower bound, not an off-by-one-tolerant one.",
    "is_error_case": true,
    "judgment_call": false
  }
],

