file.content:
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "plan@1",
  "id": "PLAN-LUMEN-001-MODEL",
  "spec_file_path": "specs/SPEC-LUMEN-001-MODEL.json",
  "linked_requirement": "REQ-LUMEN-001",
  "summary": "Implementation plan for full test coverage, versioned rate-table lookup (replacing the removed hardcoded ModelPricing match statement), per-turn token economics pricing, zero-division safety, and JSON roundtripping across lumen-model.",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "TASK-MODEL-001",
      "title": "Core Model Pricing Matrix Tests via PricingTable::rate_for & Unrecognized-Model Fallback",
      "covers_criteria": [
        "CRIT-LUMEN-002",
        "CRIT-LUMEN-003",
        "CRIT-LUMEN-004",
        "CRIT-LUMEN-008"
      ],
      "files": [
        "crates/lumen-model/tests/test_pricing.rs"
      ],
      "tdd_steps": {
        "failing_test": "Add test_core_pricing_rates_and_unrecognized_model_fallback: build PricingTable::seed(), call rate_for(\"claude-3-5-sonnet\", None, TokenRateKind::{Input,CacheWrite,CacheRead,Output}, as_of) for an as_of timestamp inside Sonnet's seeded effective window and assert $3.00/$3.75/$0.30/$15.00 per M; repeat for claude-3-5-haiku ($0.80/$1.00/$0.08/$4.00/M) and qwen-2.5-coder ($0.20/M input, $0.05/M cache read, $0.60/M output); then call rate_for(\"totally-unrecognized-model-xyz\", None, TokenRateKind::Input, as_of) (and repeat for CacheWrite/CacheRead/Output) and assert each result equals rate_for(\"claude-3-5-sonnet\", ..., same kind, as_of).",
        "expected_failure": "Fails to compile: TokenRateKind, PricingRate, PricingTable, and rate_for do not exist yet (ModelPricing and ModelPricing::from_model_name are being removed this pass, see spec scope).",
        "implementation": "Implement TokenRateKind, PricingRate, and PricingTable::seed() seeding claude-3-5-sonnet, claude-3-5-haiku, and qwen-2.5-coder rows carrying forward the exact dollar amounts from CRIT-LUMEN-002/003/004 unchanged, each row's effective_from set to a shared baseline epoch constant with effective_until None. Implement PricingTable::rate_for with the CRIT-LUMEN-008 branch: when the requested model string matches no row at all, fall back to claude-3-5-sonnet's rate for the requested kind/as_of.",
        "expected_pass": "test_core_pricing_rates_and_unrecognized_model_fallback passes with exact per-kind rates for the three recognized models and the unrecognized-model fallback confirmed equal to Sonnet's rates across every TokenRateKind."
      },
      "commit_message": "test(lumen-model): rewrite pricing matrix tests onto PricingTable::rate_for, replacing removed ModelPricing"
    },
    {
      "id": "TASK-MODEL-002",
      "title": "Token Economics Zero-Division, Savings Clamping, Percentage-Scale & Prompt Summation Tests via Per-Turn TurnPricingInput",
      "covers_criteria": [
        "CRIT-LUMEN-005",
        "CRIT-LUMEN-006",
        "CRIT-LUMEN-007",
        "CRIT-LUMEN-009",
        "CRIT-LUMEN-010"
      ],
      "files": [
        "crates/lumen-model/tests/test_pricing.rs"
      ],
      "tdd_steps": {
        "failing_test": "Add test_token_economics_zero_division_clamping_and_scale with five assertions against TokenEconomics::calculate(turns: &[TurnPricingInput], model_name, pricing: &PricingTable, provided_cost_usd: Option<f64>): (a) calculate(&[], \"claude-3-5-sonnet\", &pricing, None) asserts cache_hit_ratio == 0.0, efficiency_multiplier == 1.0, total_cost_usd == 0.0 (CRIT-007); (b) a single TurnPricingInput whose input/cache_creation/cache_read token counts are chosen so cache_read_tokens is exactly half of (input+cache_creation+cache_read) asserts cache_hit_ratio == 50.0 (not 0.5), locking in the 0-100 percentage scale (CRIT-005); (c) a turn with zero cache activity asserts net_savings_usd == 0.0 (never negative) even though baseline_cost_no_cache_usd == total_cost_usd in that case (CRIT-009); (d) TurnTokenUsage::prompt_tokens on a fixture with distinct input/cache_creation/cache_read values asserts it equals their sum (CRIT-010); (e) a mixed-cache turn asserts efficiency_multiplier == baseline_cost_no_cache_usd / total_cost_usd (CRIT-006).",
        "expected_failure": "Fails to compile: TokenEconomics::calculate's prior signature took pre-summed session totals directly, not a &[TurnPricingInput] slice plus &PricingTable and provided_cost_usd parameters.",
        "implementation": "Change TokenEconomics::calculate to accept turns: &[TurnPricingInput], model_name: &str, pricing: &PricingTable, provided_cost_usd: Option<f64>. For each turn, price it via PricingTable::rate_for(model_name, turn.tier.as_deref(), kind, turn.timestamp) per TokenRateKind and sum the per-turn costs into total_cost_usd; sum raw input_tokens/output_tokens/cache_creation_tokens/cache_read_tokens as simple totals across turns (unaffected by the pricing change). Guard cache_hit_ratio/efficiency_multiplier against zero total prompt tokens, and clamp net_savings_usd to a minimum of 0.0.",
        "expected_pass": "test_token_economics_zero_division_clamping_and_scale passes for all five assertions (a)-(e)."
      },
      "commit_message": "test(lumen-model): adapt token economics tests to per-turn TurnPricingInput pricing and lock percentage-scale cache_hit_ratio"
    },
    {
      "id": "TASK-MODEL-003",
      "title": "Canonical Transcript Full Structural Roundtrip Serialization Tests",
      "covers_criteria": [
        "CRIT-LUMEN-001"
      ],
      "files": [
        "crates/lumen-model/tests/test_transcript.rs"
      ],
      "tdd_steps": {
        "failing_test": "Add test_canonical_transcript_full_hierarchy_roundtrip verifying subagents, anomalies, schema citations, tool intents, and turn roles.",
        "expected_failure": "Tests fail if JSON serialization drops any fields or loses precision.",
        "implementation": "Validate serde attributes across CanonicalTranscript, CanonicalTurn, ToolIntent, and TrajectoryAnomaly.",
        "expected_pass": "test_canonical_transcript_full_hierarchy_roundtrip passes with identical struct equality."
      },
      "commit_message": "test(lumen-model): add exhaustive canonical transcript roundtrip test"
    },
    {
      "id": "TASK-MODEL-004",
      "title": "Extended Multi-Provider Pricing Matrix Tests via PricingTable (Opus, GPT-4o, DeepSeek, Kimi, GLM, Gemini)",
      "covers_criteria": [
        "CRIT-LUMEN-099",
        "CRIT-LUMEN-100",
        "CRIT-LUMEN-101",
        "CRIT-LUMEN-102",
        "CRIT-LUMEN-103",
        "CRIT-LUMEN-104",
        "CRIT-LUMEN-105"
      ],
      "files": [
        "crates/lumen-model/tests/test_pricing.rs"
      ],
      "tdd_steps": {
        "failing_test": "Add test_extended_pricing_matrix: for each of claude-opus, gpt-4o, deepseek-r1, kimi-k1.5, glm-4-plus, gemini-2.0-flash, gemini-2.0-pro, call PricingTable::seed().rate_for(model, None, kind, as_of) for every applicable TokenRateKind and assert the exact per-M rates from CRIT-LUMEN-099 through 105, including that TokenRateKind::CacheWrite's rate equals TokenRateKind::Input's rate for the six non-Anthropic models.",
        "expected_failure": "Fails to compile: the 7 ModelPricing constants and their fields no longer exist (ModelPricing removed this pass); PricingTable::seed() does not yet carry rows for these 7 models.",
        "implementation": "Extend PricingTable::seed() with PricingRate rows for the 7 models, carrying forward the exact CRIT-LUMEN-099-105 dollar amounts unchanged -- only their representation moves from match arms to versioned rows. Each row's effective_from uses the same baseline epoch constant introduced in TASK-MODEL-001, with effective_until None.",
        "expected_pass": "test_extended_pricing_matrix passes with exact precision for all 7 models across every applicable TokenRateKind."
      },
      "commit_message": "test(lumen-model): migrate extended multi-provider pricing matrix tests onto PricingTable rows"
    },
    {
      "id": "TASK-MODEL-005",
      "title": "PricingTable::rate_for Versioned As-Of Lookup and Deterministic Tie-Break Tests",
      "covers_criteria": [
        "CRIT-LUMEN-159"
      ],
      "files": [
        "crates/lumen-model/tests/test_pricing.rs"
      ],
      "tdd_steps": {
        "failing_test": "Add test_rate_for_versioned_lookup_and_tie_break with three scenarios against a hand-built PricingTable (not PricingTable::seed()): (a) two rows for the same (model, tier, kind) with non-overlapping consecutive [effective_from, effective_until) windows representing a price change -- rate_for with an as_of inside the first window returns the first rate, and with an as_of inside the second window returns the second rate, proving the CALLING TURN's own timestamp (not wall-clock now) selects the row; (b) two rows with identical effective_from and no effective_until (an authoring-error overlap) -- rate_for returns the rate of whichever row appears LAST in PricingTable.rates' vector declaration order; (c) two rows with different effective_from values whose windows overlap -- rate_for returns the row with the LATER effective_from.",
        "expected_failure": "Fails to compile or fails scenario (b)/(c): rate_for does not exist yet, or an initial naive linear-scan implementation returns the FIRST matching row instead of applying the effective_from-then-declaration-order tie-break.",
        "implementation": "Implement PricingTable::rate_for to filter rows by (model, tier, kind) and by as_of within [effective_from, effective_until) (effective_until == None treated as unbounded), then among matches select by maximum effective_from, breaking ties by the LATEST index in PricingTable.rates.",
        "expected_pass": "test_rate_for_versioned_lookup_and_tie_break passes for all three window/tie-break scenarios (a)-(c)."
      },
      "commit_message": "test(lumen-model): verify PricingTable::rate_for as-of window selection and deterministic tie-break ordering"
    },
    {
      "id": "TASK-MODEL-006",
      "title": "Recognized-Model Missing-Rate-Kind Returns 0.0, Not Sonnet Fallback",
      "covers_criteria": [
        "CRIT-LUMEN-161"
      ],
      "files": [
        "crates/lumen-model/tests/test_pricing.rs"
      ],
      "tdd_steps": {
        "failing_test": "Add test_recognized_model_missing_kind_returns_zero: build a PricingTable seeded with qwen-2.5-coder rows for Input/CacheRead/Output only (no CacheWrite row, matching CRIT-LUMEN-004's real gap -- Qwen has no seeded cache-write price), call rate_for(\"qwen-2.5-coder\", None, TokenRateKind::CacheWrite, as_of) and assert it returns exactly 0.0, and explicitly assert the result is NOT equal to claude-3-5-sonnet's $3.75/M CacheWrite rate -- distinguishing this recognized-model/missing-kind case from the CRIT-LUMEN-008 unrecognized-model fallback path covered in TASK-MODEL-001.",
        "expected_failure": "Fails if rate_for falls back to Sonnet's (or any other model's) CacheWrite rate for a recognized model's genuinely-absent rate kind, or if it panics instead of returning 0.0.",
        "implementation": "In PricingTable::rate_for, first check whether the model string matches at least one row at all (recognized). If recognized, search only that model's rows for the requested (tier, kind, as_of); if none match, return 0.0 directly without falling through to the CRIT-LUMEN-008 unrecognized-model-wide fallback branch, which only triggers when the model matches zero rows.",
        "expected_pass": "test_recognized_model_missing_kind_returns_zero passes, confirming 0.0 is returned and no other model's rate is substituted."
      },
      "commit_message": "test(lumen-model): verify recognized model with missing rate kind returns 0.0 instead of Sonnet fallback"
    },
    {
      "id": "TASK-MODEL-007",
      "title": "provided_cost_usd Twin-Field Verbatim Storage and Non-Override Tests",
      "covers_criteria": [
        "CRIT-LUMEN-160"
      ],
      "files": [
        "crates/lumen-model/tests/test_pricing.rs"
      ],
      "tdd_steps": {
        "failing_test": "Add test_provided_cost_usd_twin_field: (a) build a turns fixture whose independently-computed cost does NOT equal 4.20, call TokenEconomics::calculate(&turns, model, &pricing, Some(4.20)), and assert provided_cost_usd == Some(4.20) while total_cost_usd is the independently computed value -- proving the two differ and neither overrides nor blends with the other; (b) call TokenEconomics::calculate(&turns, model, &pricing, None) and assert provided_cost_usd == None, not Some(0.0).",
        "expected_failure": "Fails to compile: TokenEconomics has no provided_cost_usd field yet and TokenEconomics::calculate takes no provided_cost_usd parameter.",
        "implementation": "Add provided_cost_usd: Option<f64> to TokenEconomics. Thread the provided_cost_usd parameter of TokenEconomics::calculate straight into the returned struct's field verbatim, with total_cost_usd computed independently from turns/pricing with no reference to provided_cost_usd.",
        "expected_pass": "test_provided_cost_usd_twin_field passes: provided_cost_usd stores the caller's value verbatim, defaults to None when absent, and total_cost_usd is unaffected by its presence or value."
      },
      "commit_message": "test(lumen-model): verify provided_cost_usd is stored verbatim and never overrides computed total_cost_usd"
    }
  ]
}

